From 58e6bfa4e77c1efc6065c9b07d47c7d68fdaff36
Subject: Mirror RenderMeshInstances/RenderMaterialInstances into render-entity components
Origin: https://github.com/robtfm/bevy/commit/58e6bfa4e77c1efc6065c9b07d47c7d68fdaff36
Date: 2026-07-06T14:03:47+01:00

Genesis Plaza on wasm is main-thread CPU-bound, with ~37% of frame time in
MainEntity-keyed hashmap probes re-run per entity per phase per view from the
specialize/queue/draw paths. Mirror the two hottest maps into components on
render-world entities and convert the hot readers to component-first lookups
(archetype row access) with map fallback:

- Mesh3d entities sync to the render world (SyncComponentPlugin) so they have
  render-world counterparts to carry the mirrors
- RenderMeshInstanceGpuC mirrors the RenderMeshInstances GPU-building map;
  RenderMaterialInstanceC mirrors RenderMaterialInstances
- MeshInstanceLookup / MaterialInstanceLookup SystemParams wrap the lookups;
  specialize/queue for material, prepass and shadows, plus DrawMesh,
  SetMeshBindGroup and SetMaterialBindGroup are converted
- RenderBin stores the representative render entity (BinEntry) so per-draw
  lookups on binned batches hit the component path instead of PLACEHOLDER
- extraction re-mirrors on Changed<RenderEntity> to survive render-entity
  replacement (synced-component removal from a live entity)

The maps remain authoritative and their public API is unchanged, so external
consumers (e.g. boimp) are unaffected. A new validate_instance_mirror cargo
feature adds probe-time equivalence asserts and per-frame map<->component
symmetry sweeps for validation builds.

Measured (wasm, Genesis Plaza, fixed viewpoint): hashmap self-time 37.8% ->
27.5% of main-thread time; the two converted maps 14.7% -> 1.1%.

NOTE: THROWAWAY on migration to bevy >= 0.19. Upstream #22966 ("change lists
instead of ticks") restructures visibility/specialize/queue so these
per-entity probes disappear entirely. Drop this commit when rebasing; do not
port it.
